  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The last update had an odd affect on face mirror. \n\n- Faces appear stretched, flattened out, or very wide\n\n- The camera principal point/ focus point is centered on the face when zoomed in, but when zooming out, the viewpoint center shifts lower and lower, eventually causing half of the face mirror to be the avatars chest. This means any avatar with larger than human ears (or a hat, big hair, etc.) will have them cropped off when zoomed in, while if you zoom out, half of the face mirror ends up being your avatars chest, and even your arms become visible. This makes it very hard or impossible to actually have a proper face view.  \n\nFix - Make principal point the face, or enable a vertical slider adjust for the face mirror.",
